 "final_passage": "On the Halvard-Parl English→Estonian test set, Tessaline achieves a mean BLEU of 28.4 ± 0.6 over 8 seeds, compared to 27.6 ± 0.8 for Varrow-NMT, a statistically significant mean paired difference of 0.8 BLEU points (95% CI [0.2, 1.44], p = 0.017, paired t-test). Tessaline also substantially outperforms the PhraseGrid reference baseline, with a mean BLEU of 22.1 ± 0.8 and a statistically significant mean paired difference of 6.3 BLEU points (95% CI [5.87, 6.83], p < 0.001, paired t-test). The improvement over Varrow-NMT is small in magnitude relative to the gap over the phrase-based baseline, and these results are limited to this single test set and language pair.",
